      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the equation of the line parameterized by \\( t \\) given the points on the line at specific values of \\( t \\). The general form of a line parameterized by \\( t \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\mathbf{r}_0 + (t - t_0) \\mathbf{d}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( \\mathbf{r}_0 \\) is a point on the line (the position vector at \\( t = t_0 \\)), \\( t_0 \\) is a time parameter, and \\( \\mathbf{d} \\) is the direction vector of the line.\n\nWe know two points on the line:\n1. When \\( t = 2 \\), the vector on the line is \\( \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} \\).\n2. When \\( t = 3 \\), the vector on the line is \\( \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix} \\).\n\nFirst, we need to find the direction vector \\( \\mathbf{d} \\). Let \\( t_0 = 2 \\) and the point on the line at \\( t = 2 \\) be \\( \\mathbf{r}_0 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} \\). The direction vector \\( \\mathbf{d} \\) can be found by subtracting the vector at \\( t = 2 \\) from the vector at \\( t = 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{d} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 - 1 \\\\ -4 - 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSo, the direction vector is \\( \\mathbf{d} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix} \\). Now we know that when \\( t = 2 \\), the vector is \\( \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} \\), and the direction vector \\( \\mathbf{d} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix} \\). The equation of the line is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + (t - 2) \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the vector on the line at \\( t = -7 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(-7) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + (-7 - 2) \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + (-9) \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(-7) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} -18 \\\\ 72 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 - 18 \\\\ 4 + 72 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -17 \\\\ 76 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the vector on the line at \\( t = -7 \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -17 \\\\ 76 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]",
